  But getting back to the original topic (or "no'i", as we say in lojban
:-) ), my five kids know a little lojban vocabulary  (the numbers and many
colors and a few other words like gerku, zdani, and cutci) but on the whole
never had an interest in it. (Heck, my middle kid  even had "1 hour lojban
lesson" as one of the birthday copupons he gave me)   My youngest when
already born by the time I started learning lojban, and my wife would in no
way let me use her as a guinea pig (Robin's lucky ;-) ) My dogs, however,
know a few lojban commands ("ko zutse", "ko vreta", "ko klama mi", "ko
klama fi mi")
         00gejyspa


